14	/// ## What it does
15	/// Checks for duplicate union members.
16	///
17	/// ## Why is this bad?
18	/// Duplicate union members are redundant and should be removed.
19	///
20	/// ## Example
21	/// ```python
22	/// foo: str | str
23	/// ```
24	///
25	/// Use instead:
26	/// ```python
27	/// foo: str
28	/// ```
29	///
30	/// ## Fix safety
31	/// This rule's fix is marked as safe unless the union contains comments.
32	///
33	/// For nested union, the fix will flatten type expressions into a single
34	/// top-level union.
35	///
36	/// ## References
37	/// - [Python documentation: `typing.Union`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Union)
